--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

agent-media *drives* several third-party programs; it does not bundle or link
them, and their licences do not reach this repository's code. Each runs as a
separate process, reached over an IPC socket, HTTP, or the command line:

  mpv           GPLv2-or-later    playback engine (driven over JSON IPC)
  Mopidy / MPD  Apache-2.0 / GPL  library + queue on the rooms lane
  yt-dlp        Unlicense         acquisition, run on the phone
  Snapcast      GPLv3             whole-house sync (currently disabled)
  Termux:API    GPLv3             phone sensors and notifications

This matters if the Android companion in `android/` ever *bundles* libmpv
rather than talking to a separately-installed mpv over TCP, as it does today:
linking libmpv would make the app a derivative work of a GPL program, and the
app would have to be licensed accordingly. Keeping mpv at arm's length is a
deliberate architectural choice, not an accident — see
docs/proposals/2026-08-13-android-companion-app.md.

